# Weekly blog system (research → 3 drafts)

When the user asks to run the **weekly blog**, **Sunday blog**, **blog drafts**, or Abacus-style research:

1. Follow **`tools/weekly-blog-system-rules.md`** end-to-end (source of truth).
2. News window: `START_DATE = TODAY−7` through `END_DATE = TODAY−1` (evergreen exempt).
3. Categories: (1) final expense & funeral costs, (2) term life, (3) whole life, (4) approved-carrier consumer product news, (5) scams/consumer protection. SEO priority: **final expense → term life → whole life**. **That is the only topical focus.**
4. **Consumer only** — never agent/IMO/producer framing. **Spanish SEO first** (EN drafts → ES publish indexed; EN pages `noindex`).
5. **No Medicare/Medigap/IUL/VUL/LTC/industry-trade focus.** Brief “Medicare doesn’t pay funerals” lines OK inside FE articles only.
6. Story Fit Test: useful for clients/future clients + SEO. **Do not exclude by state** (NE/KS/CO/NV are priority, not a ban). **Do not exclude by publisher/source**.
7. Hard limits only: no competitor names in drafts, no IUL/VUL/variable, no auto/home as main topic, Category 4 = Assurity / Mutual of Omaha / American Amicable / Corebridge / Transamerica / Aetna only.
8. Evergreen: use Section 6.2 gap topics only; never duplicate `tools/blog-drafts/shared/covered-evergreen-topics.md`.
9. Deliver **exactly 3** English drafts (600–900 words), 5-section structure, CTA `1-402-440-5438`. Save under `tools/blog-drafts/`. Do not publish until Julie asks.
10. After publish request: digest = condensed 150–250 words/story; full-article pages = **same ~600–900 word depth as the emailed drafts** (ES + EN parity). Follow `newsletter-consumer-blog.mdc` + `blog-build-rules.md` (Spanish index only; FAQ; no template leftovers). Only sitemap/`index` weeks that pass the consumer FE/term/whole bar.

Mutual of Omaha (carrier) OK; **Mutual of Omaha Direct** never.
